-- title:
--   Non-zero ℓ-torsion in a cyclic group has ℓ-1 elements
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be an additive abelian group (in the universe `Type`) that is cyclic, i.e. generated by a single element. Let $m$ be a natural number with $\operatorname{Nat.card} D = m$ and $m \neq 0$, so that $D$ is finite of order $m$. Let $\ell$ be a prime natural number dividing $m$. The assertion is that the set of $x \in D$ satisfying simultaneously $\ell \cdot x = 0$ and $x \neq 0$ has cardinality (in the sense of `Set.ncard`) exactly $\ell - 1$, the subtraction being truncated subtraction of natural numbers. In other words, a finite cyclic group whose order is divisible by the prime $\ell$ contains precisely $\ell - 1$ non-zero elements annihilated by $\ell$, these being the non-identity elements of its unique subgroup of order $\ell$.
--
--   This is the elementary torsion count for cyclic groups: the $\ell$-torsion subgroup of a cyclic group of order divisible by $\ell$ is cyclic of order $\ell$, so it has $\ell-1$ non-zero elements. It is used in the modular-curve part of the development, in the orbit count [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.two_mul_index_gammaH_sup_zpowers_neg_one_le_ncard_orbit_gamma1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.two_mul_index_gammaH_sup_zpowers_neg_one_le_ncard_orbit_gamma1), where points of exact order $\ell$ on a cyclic group furnish the $\Gamma_1$-level data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsAddCyclic_ncard_setOf_nsmul_eq_zero_and_ne_zero_of_prime_dvd_card.lean

